[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Out of Control]
[00:12.74]What was the danger?
[00:16.87]As the man tried to swing the speedboat round, the steering wheel came away in his hands.
[00:24.47]He waved desperately to his companion, who had been water skiing for the last fifteen minutes.
[00:31.79]Both men had hardly had time to realize what was happening when they were thrown violently into the sea.
[00:40.18]The speedboat had struck a buoy, but it continued to move very quickly across the water.
[00:48.09]Both men had just begun to swim towards the shore,
[00:52.42]when they noticed with dismay that the speedboat was moving in a circle.
[00:57.60]It now came straight towards them at tremendous speed.
[01:02.52]In less than a minute, it roared past them only a few feet away.
[01:09.11]After it had passed,
[01:11.11]they swam on as quickly as they could because they knew that the boat would soon return.
[01:17.54]They had just had enough time to swim out of danger when the boat again completed a circle.
[01:26.21]On this occasion, however, it had slowed down considerably.
[01:31.86]The petrol had nearly all been used up.
[01:35.57]Before long, the noise dropped completely and the boat began to drift gently across the water.
